@guidance text/markdown spec/initial.md
---
[contract-gate] Anchor contract gate (reviewing)
Files: proposals/semantic-contract.md; proposals/cellular-automata-anchor.md; spec/initial.md
Do: Freeze the anchor decisions that are already settled: one-second game ticks, arbitrary continuous t_ sampling, empty journal as empty set, journal-owned saucer creation, postdated entries, three layers, direct indexed queries, and SDK/game-object separation. Record only the remaining implementation-level choices.
Accept: The implementation packets can consume one coherent contract without importing the removed interval-fold model.
> Anchor game tick period is one second of logical time; LogicalTime/Tau may use finer fixed-point resolution independently of the game tick.
> An entry is visible at its exact timestamp. A journal entry inside a game tick participates in automaton behavior at the next tick boundary; an entry exactly on a tick boundary participates in that tick.
> Before CreateSaucer is visible, the journal query returns the empty set. CreateSaucer at t_=0 establishes the 91-tile saucer.
> A postdated entry may be authored into the immutable journal before evaluation; queries ignore entries after their requested t_.
> Acts, moves, destroys, ignites, and converts are indexed differences between returned values, never mutation or actor execution.
---
[workspace-time] Workspace and time module (reviewing)
Files: Cargo.toml; crates/engine-time/**
Do: Bootstrap the Rust workspace and implement distinct LogicalTime and Tau wrappers with the approved signed i64 representation, one-second anchor game-tick relation, checked arithmetic, ordering, and exact equality. Keep raw time arithmetic in this crate.
Accept: Boundary and overflow tests pass; no game-domain types or evaluator logic are owned here.
-> contract-gate
