[indexed-query] Direct indexed query kernel (reviewing)
Files: crates/engine-index/**; consume engine-time, engine-sdk, engine-journal, caravan-domain
Do: Implement the generic direct query boundary: select the game-tick index from t_, expose journal entries visible at t_, and return a new GameState without prior-state input, stepping API, or evaluator-owned RNG. Keep the query generic over game payloads and define the extension point the Caravan reference oracle will use.
Accept: Empty journal, saucer creation, postdated entries, arbitrary query order, within-tick stability under a fixed journal, and journal-time discontinuities are testable. No current-state or interval callback API is introduced.
-> domain-model
-> journal-writer
-> sdk-envelopes
> For a fixed immutable worldline, automaton-derived data is stable between game-tick boundaries unless a visible journal entry creates an exact-time discontinuity.
> The query never advances a current state, observes a prior query, or causes an actor to act.
@artifact text/plain crates/engine-index/src/lib.rs
